  "comment": "About 160 Central Florida species: the 150 bird species with the most research-grade iNaturalist observations created up to 2026-09-27 across Orange (934), Seminole (392), Osceola (938), Lake (534), Polk (948: Circle B Bar Reserve) and Brevard (839: Merritt Island, Viera Wetlands) Counties, then the October and November top 120 (the wintering ducks and the fall migrants a yearly ranking buries), then birds heard more than seen (Carolina Chickadee, Eastern Screech Owl, Clapper, King and Virginia Rails, Bachman's Sparrow, Brown-headed Nuthatch and the rest already in). Feral Muscovy Ducks, Egyptian Geese and Indian Peafowl stay in: they are what one meets in Orlando. `packbuilder draft --place 934 --place 392 --place 938 --place 534 --place 948 --place 839 --before 2026-09-27 --top 150 --season 10,11 --season-top 120 --add ...`. scientific_name and common_name follow the BirdNET+ label file as in us-ca-la (species the committed packs already list reuse their entries); inat_taxon_id is iNaturalist's; wikipedia_url is iNaturalist's link for the taxon. The order is the observation ranking, then the species added by hand. Drafted with `packbuilder draft` (the command is below) and read over by a person; tests/test_definition.py checks the labels.",
